WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.919
- If I could switch wine cellars
with any player in a one-

00:00:02.919 --> 00:00:06.047
on-one game, I would switch with—

00:00:06.047 --> 00:00:08.258
- Take a little sip on that one.

00:00:08.258 --> 00:00:10.051
- I got to take a sip on that one.

00:00:10.051 --> 00:00:13.471
Who do you think's got a
better wine cellar: JJ [Redick] or Jimmy Butler?

00:00:13.471 --> 00:00:16.307
- Jimmy Butler has the most
diversity in his cellar.

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:17.851
I'm not going to
beat him one-on-one,

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:18.601
but if I could...

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:33.783
We are here on Full-Bodied
today with the pride and joy

00:00:33.783 --> 00:00:36.953
of the Lehigh Mountain
Hawks; the man, the myth,

00:00:36.953 --> 00:00:38.788
the legend of the
Portland Trail Blazers;

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:41.666
the skills and drills
master, CJ McCollum.

00:00:41.666 --> 00:00:43.418
Thank you again for
coming in and having

00:00:43.418 --> 00:00:45.795
a glass or glasses with us.

00:00:45.795 --> 00:00:48.965
So all three of these wines
meant something not only to me

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:52.469
in my story to you, but
I felt like in relation

00:00:52.469 --> 00:00:54.554
to your story, your life story.

00:00:54.554 --> 00:00:57.724
Let's start with
your wine first.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.643
You know how the game is a
business. At the same time, how

00:01:00.643 --> 00:01:03.146
have you dealt with
not only trade rumors,

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:06.649
but maybe sometimes not
always getting the credit you have

00:01:06.649 --> 00:01:09.194
deserved for evolving your game?

00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:12.989
- To start with development, it's
just been the story of my life.

00:01:12.989 --> 00:01:14.657
Just work hard, work
for what you want

00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:16.576
and kind of continue to
have to prove yourself

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:17.535
over and over again.

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:19.454
As I continued to work
and finally got a chance,

00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:20.705
I just didn't want to blow it.

00:01:20.705 --> 00:01:22.665
And I think throughout
the course of my career,

00:01:22.665 --> 00:01:25.168
I've had to kind of reinvent
myself and kind of prove myself

00:01:25.168 --> 00:01:25.668
each year.

00:01:25.668 --> 00:01:28.922
Prove my consistency, prove I
can score first at this level,

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:31.091
then prove I can be a
facilitator at this level.

00:01:31.091 --> 00:01:34.135
And I think eight years later,
five years as a starter, Dame

00:01:34.135 --> 00:01:36.805
and I have been able to make the
playoffs seven straight years.

00:01:36.805 --> 00:01:38.181
We've been able
to coexist, we've

00:01:38.181 --> 00:01:40.683
been able to thrive together,
empower each other, and my game

00:01:40.683 --> 00:01:42.852
has evolved to the
point where this year,

00:01:42.852 --> 00:01:44.187
and obviously before I got hurt,

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:46.397
I was shooting 10,
11 threes a game, hitting

00:01:46.397 --> 00:01:48.024
four or five threes a night.

00:01:48.024 --> 00:01:49.651
I was averaging five assists.

00:01:49.651 --> 00:01:51.194
I was helping lead
our team in a lot

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:52.654
of different
statistical categories

00:01:52.654 --> 00:01:54.364
but also from a
leadership standpoint.

00:01:54.364 --> 00:01:56.324
- You were balling,
now. You was different.

00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:58.076
Let me give you
credit because you've

00:01:58.076 --> 00:02:00.161
taken your role
of leadership. I'm

00:02:00.161 --> 00:02:03.331
like, dang, like, this dude is
taking it to the next level.

00:02:03.331 --> 00:02:04.916
Something to correlate
that to your wine,

00:02:04.916 --> 00:02:08.586
I think to have the opportunity
to be in this business

00:02:08.586 --> 00:02:11.214
and to not only put your
signature on your wine

00:02:11.214 --> 00:02:13.466
but to make sure that you're
trying to get better at it

00:02:13.466 --> 00:02:15.760
every single day is
ridiculously tight,

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:19.472
and I'm pretty excited to be
in this business with you.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:23.017
If you had to play somebody one-
on-one for their wine cellar,

00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:23.726
who would it be?

00:02:23.726 --> 00:02:27.856
- Ooh. Hmm.

00:02:27.856 --> 00:02:30.483
- You got to take a
little sip on that one.

00:02:30.483 --> 00:02:32.110
- I got to take a sip on that one.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:36.447
If I could switch wine cellars
with any player in a one-

00:02:36.447 --> 00:02:38.867
on-one game, I
would switch with—

00:02:38.867 --> 00:02:40.952
who do you think’s got
a better wine cellar?

00:02:40.952 --> 00:02:42.370
JJ or Jimmy Butler?

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:45.373
- Jimmy Butler has the most
diversity in his cellar.

00:02:45.373 --> 00:02:48.251
I'm not going to beat him one-
on-one, but if I could—right?—

00:02:48.251 --> 00:02:49.669
I would get his cellar.

00:02:49.669 --> 00:02:49.711
I like somebody where you could
say what part of the world

00:02:49.711 --> 00:02:51.629
I like somebody where you could
say what part of the world

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:52.797
do you want to go to?

00:02:52.797 --> 00:02:54.549
Do you have a Riesling
in your cellar?

00:02:54.549 --> 00:02:56.926
Do you have a Chilean
wine in your cellar?

00:02:56.926 --> 00:02:59.637
Do you have some New Worlds,
you know, Sonoma Coast?

00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:03.474
Do you have some Walla Walla
Merlot or some Red Mountain

00:03:03.474 --> 00:03:06.144
Cabernet from Washington.
So that is what I like.

00:03:06.144 --> 00:03:06.394
Like, wine is so vast.

00:03:06.394 --> 00:03:07.687
Like, wine is so vast.

00:03:07.687 --> 00:03:09.314
- That's why I mentioned
Jimmy because I

00:03:09.314 --> 00:03:12.483
know he's well-versed in
traveling throughout Europe

00:03:12.483 --> 00:03:13.568
and being in France.

00:03:13.568 --> 00:03:14.319
- Oh, for sure.

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:16.112
- Being in some of these
areas, so he would bring me,

00:03:16.112 --> 00:03:18.239
he would expose me to some
things I haven't tasted.

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:19.032
Like, Melo loves white Burgundy.

00:03:19.741 --> 00:03:20.783
JJ loves white Burgundy.

00:03:20.783 --> 00:03:22.368
They got a nice
mixture of things

00:03:22.368 --> 00:03:24.370
that I wouldn't normally
have in my rotation.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:24.579
that I wouldn't normally
have in my rotation.

00:03:24.579 --> 00:03:27.457
- Describe these players
with specifically

00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:30.585
the bottle or varietal of wine.
- Wow.

00:03:30.585 --> 00:03:32.378
- So we're going to
start with LeBron.

00:03:32.378 --> 00:03:35.882
- Wow, man. He's like, I
mean, what would you want?

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.926
American? You want Burgundy?

00:03:37.926 --> 00:03:38.426
- No, no, no.

00:03:38.426 --> 00:03:39.344
Worldly. Worldly.

00:03:39.344 --> 00:03:40.553
We can go all over the world.

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:41.221
I'm with you.

00:03:41.221 --> 00:03:43.056
- You know, you got Bron,
who’s arguably the best

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.265
player to ever play the game.

00:03:44.265 --> 00:03:47.810
So, like, depending on what
your favorite wine is that exists,

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:50.563
I mean, he's a
Chateau Margaux, man,

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.983
in terms of what I would
drink. He was great early.

00:03:53.983 --> 00:03:55.276
You know, he was deemed The
Chosen One, and he's

00:03:57.278 --> 00:04:00.240
been able to kind of extend his
career 18 years later to where

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.282
he's sharper.

00:04:01.282 --> 00:04:03.493
He's a better jump-shooter
than he was when he first

00:04:03.493 --> 00:04:04.369
got into the league.

00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:06.663
Still able to empower his
teammates, still able to make

00:04:06.663 --> 00:04:09.249
his team win and still—
depending on who you argue with—

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:10.750
is still the best
player in the NBA.

00:04:10.750 --> 00:04:14.504
So I think from a
price-point standpoint,

00:04:14.504 --> 00:04:17.757
you looked at Top Shot, you see
how he's moving the needle.

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:18.466
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:18.466 --> 00:04:20.635
- Trading cards,
everything in that realm,

00:04:20.635 --> 00:04:22.095
and then it's impact
off the court.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.846
I think you look
at wines and what

00:04:23.846 --> 00:04:25.598
they've been able
to do for people,

00:04:25.598 --> 00:04:27.433
you talked about bringing
families together,

00:04:27.433 --> 00:04:29.227
being able to gift
people wines, share

00:04:29.227 --> 00:04:30.603
wines with certain people.

00:04:30.603 --> 00:04:34.315
I think he's done the same
thing with his platform.

00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:36.943
He's shared to
communities, he shared

00:04:36.943 --> 00:04:39.070
to the kids that come
from where we come from.

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.863
So I would say he's top-shelf.

00:04:40.863 --> 00:04:43.658
He's the type of wine that
you know your wife won't

00:04:43.658 --> 00:04:46.536
touch while you're out of town.

00:04:46.536 --> 00:04:48.204
- All right, so how
about I'm going

00:04:48.204 --> 00:04:50.873
to go to young
fella LaMelo Ball.

00:04:50.873 --> 00:04:55.003
- LaMelo Ball, he is probably,
I mean, definitely New World.

00:04:55.003 --> 00:04:55.962
- OK. OK.

00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.672
He's so young, you
know what I mean.

00:04:57.672 --> 00:05:01.259
He's got potential to be like
Opus, you know what I mean.
- Ooh.

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:02.927
- Yeah, I said it. He's
got the potential

00:05:02.927 --> 00:05:07.724
to be Opus. The ceiling is very,
very high, a lot of upside.

00:05:07.724 --> 00:05:09.851
I would definitely say the
acidity levels are high.

00:05:09.851 --> 00:05:11.352
- [Laughing]

00:05:11.352 --> 00:05:14.063
- You know, the game is like,
it leaves you like “wow.”

00:05:16.941 --> 00:05:19.360
He's ahead of his time
from a vision standpoint.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:21.070
When Mike [Jordan] is
saying that he's better

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.865
than we thought, you know you're
doing what you supposed to do.

00:05:24.282 --> 00:05:26.159
- Let's go to the next one, right?

00:05:26.159 --> 00:05:29.787
And I think the next
one would be my wine.

00:05:29.787 --> 00:05:33.458
You are really good at a lot
of things outside of basketball,

00:05:33.458 --> 00:05:35.793
whether you're the vice
president of the NBPA, whether you're

00:05:35.793 --> 00:05:38.087
doing stuff when it comes
to Bitcoin and NFTs,

00:05:38.087 --> 00:05:40.340
whether you're doing the
mental health, whether you're

00:05:40.340 --> 00:05:41.382
doing a show.

00:05:41.382 --> 00:05:43.259
So how do you do that?

00:05:43.259 --> 00:05:45.386
Like, how do you find
time for all these things,

00:05:45.386 --> 00:05:47.597
and what is your motivation
to being like that?

00:05:47.597 --> 00:05:50.016
Is there a question to
kids who are 14 or 15

00:05:50.016 --> 00:05:52.810
where people tell them
just stick to basketball?

00:05:52.810 --> 00:05:54.604
- Basketball has
always been an escape,

00:05:54.604 --> 00:05:56.230
and I've always wanted
to use the game.

00:05:56.230 --> 00:05:58.983
I think a lot of times we allow
the game to use us, right?

00:05:58.983 --> 00:06:00.777
You know, we put our
heart and soul into it.

00:06:00.777 --> 00:06:02.487
We don't really have plans on

00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:04.072
what we're like
outside of basketball.

00:06:04.072 --> 00:06:06.324
We have no identity outside
of basketball, and then

00:06:06.324 --> 00:06:07.825
when it stops, we struggle.

00:06:07.825 --> 00:06:10.161
We struggle financially
or we struggle mentally.

00:06:10.161 --> 00:06:12.246
We struggle physically
from an exercise standpoint

00:06:12.246 --> 00:06:15.416
because we've depended on sport
for so long. We have nothing.

00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:17.460
Being a guy who didn't
have a lot of scholarships,

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:21.130
was able to go to a school
like Lehigh, get a degree and pursue

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:22.090
a career in journalism,

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:25.176
I just wanted to make sure
that I had everything in place

00:06:25.176 --> 00:06:27.136
outside of basketball as well.

00:06:27.136 --> 00:06:28.054
- Right, totally.

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.847
- Basketball has
always been my Plan A,

00:06:29.847 --> 00:06:32.433
but my Plan A involved
using basketball

00:06:32.433 --> 00:06:37.105
to get Plan B: podcast. Plan C:
sharpen up my college degree

00:06:37.105 --> 00:06:38.648
from a journalism standpoint.

00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:42.443
Part D: make sure I'm exposing
myself to different avenues

00:06:42.443 --> 00:06:44.195
so that I have different
streams of income.

00:06:44.195 --> 00:06:46.906
I think for the
14- or 15-year-old

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:48.491
that's listening
to this, people are

00:06:48.491 --> 00:06:50.159
going to tell you a lot
of things aren't possible.

00:06:50.159 --> 00:06:51.869
They're going to tell
you a lot of things

00:06:51.869 --> 00:06:54.247
can't happen to you because
it didn't happen for them.

00:06:54.247 --> 00:06:58.209
- Let's go to that last
wine. That's Alexana.

00:06:58.209 --> 00:07:00.253
You know, journeys have
to begin somewhere,

00:07:00.253 --> 00:07:02.380
and this summer actually
I had a chance to come here.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:03.506
Because some people
can make wine,

00:07:03.506 --> 00:07:05.967
but there's other people that
put passion inside their wine,

00:07:05.967 --> 00:07:07.135
which makes it taste better.

00:07:07.135 --> 00:07:11.431
And so I liken this to you as
like they just don't do wine

00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:13.349
from the Willamette
Valley. They do

00:07:13.349 --> 00:07:16.352
a little wine from Argentina,
they do some stuff from Napa,

00:07:16.352 --> 00:07:19.063
they make a Riesling,
which is next level here.

00:07:19.063 --> 00:07:23.359
But you, you do different things
at a top level, and one thing

00:07:23.359 --> 00:07:27.363
that's new that I try to explain
to people is the NBA Top Shot.

00:07:27.363 --> 00:07:30.283
And so from your perspective,
where is that going?

00:07:30.283 --> 00:07:31.951
How is that evolving?

00:07:31.951 --> 00:07:33.703
- People are starting
to learn more about it,

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:37.081
the highlight factor, and
I would have likened it

00:07:37.081 --> 00:07:38.708
to...it's similar to
the trading card

00:07:38.708 --> 00:07:42.378
industry in which the
quantity kind of determines

00:07:42.378 --> 00:07:45.298
the quality a lot of times.

00:07:45.298 --> 00:07:47.133
This is a LeBron
dunk on Jason Terry.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:49.469
Do they only make
five of them, or do they

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:50.595
make 20 of them?

00:07:50.595 --> 00:07:52.930
Yeah, like that
was an iconic play.

00:07:52.930 --> 00:07:55.933
It was like a once-in-a-lifetime
situation to which if Top

00:07:55.933 --> 00:07:59.562
Shot puts that out, I bet you
they probably only put 23 out.

00:07:59.562 --> 00:08:01.814
For one, because he's
number 23, and for two,

00:08:01.814 --> 00:08:04.358
because it's an iconic moment,
and that kind of drives

00:08:04.358 --> 00:08:05.109
the market value.

00:08:05.109 --> 00:08:07.612
But I think Top
Shot is the future.

00:08:07.612 --> 00:08:09.489
I think NFT is the
future, and being

00:08:09.489 --> 00:08:13.493
able to have a collection
that you can store online that

00:08:13.493 --> 00:08:16.287
can be safe and encrypted
is much easier

00:08:16.287 --> 00:08:18.998
than me trying to remember
trading cards that I had

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:20.124
when I was [inaudible] years old.

00:08:20.124 --> 00:08:24.253
So I think this new space of
being able to store things

00:08:24.253 --> 00:08:26.255
online in general is the way.

00:08:26.255 --> 00:08:27.882
I think NFT is the
future when you

00:08:27.882 --> 00:08:29.467
find the right
products to buy, and I

00:08:29.467 --> 00:08:32.887
think Top Shot is smart
for capitalizing on sports.

00:08:32.887 --> 00:08:35.139
It sucks that I have to
pay for my own moments.
- [Laughing]

00:08:35.139 --> 00:08:37.600
- You know what I mean? Like, I'm
trying to buy, like, my moment.

00:08:37.600 --> 00:08:40.311
Like, my pull-up,
which is crazy.

00:08:40.311 --> 00:08:44.357
- So we wanted to do a
small little game, right?

00:08:44.357 --> 00:08:46.025
And those have been
already poured.

00:08:46.025 --> 00:08:48.569
- I'm ain’t gonna lie to you, I'm
not very good at these games.

00:08:48.569 --> 00:08:49.695
- That's all right. It’s taped.

00:08:49.695 --> 00:08:51.656
- I will tell you that I did a
blind tasting with Melo,

00:08:51.656 --> 00:08:54.825
and he had the year down.
We actually went to Alexana,

00:08:54.825 --> 00:08:56.619
and he was getting the years.

00:08:56.619 --> 00:08:57.411
- Oh, was he?

00:08:57.411 --> 00:08:59.288
- One of these isn't from
Oregon or two of them

00:08:59.288 --> 00:09:00.414
aren’t from Oregon?

00:09:00.414 --> 00:09:02.124
- Well, you got to figure it out.

00:09:02.124 --> 00:09:05.294
- This one is not from
Oregon for sure.

00:09:05.294 --> 00:09:09.006
- I know what I just had
is definitely a Pinot.

00:09:09.006 --> 00:09:10.716
- This is not from here.

00:09:10.716 --> 00:09:14.053
I don't know where it's from,
but it isn’t from here.

00:09:14.053 --> 00:09:16.305
- You know what's crazy,
I can almost tell you.

00:09:16.305 --> 00:09:18.808
Oh, no, it's definitely
not a Pinot.

00:09:18.808 --> 00:09:22.979
Oh. This is the Oregon Pinot.

00:09:22.979 --> 00:09:26.566
Wow, that has a lot
of talents, but I still

00:09:26.566 --> 00:09:28.276
don't think it's old world wine.

00:09:28.276 --> 00:09:29.151
- Did you do the swish?

00:09:29.151 --> 00:09:30.653
- Oh, yeah. you have
to do the swish.

00:09:30.653 --> 00:09:32.530
You got to feel that
grip on the teeth.

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:34.365
I'm just going to say
that is the Oregon

00:09:34.365 --> 00:09:35.741
Pinot right there, right?

00:09:35.741 --> 00:09:36.284
Like Oregon--

00:09:36.284 --> 00:09:36.742
- This is from somewhere else.

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:38.286
This is from another country.

00:09:38.286 --> 00:09:40.955
- Yeah, yeah. This one's
definitely from another country.

00:09:40.955 --> 00:09:44.417
We all agreed that the
second one is a Pinot.

00:09:44.417 --> 00:09:48.671
One of them is not from America,
and the other one has to be—

00:09:48.671 --> 00:09:50.298
- I think one of them might be a Cab?

00:09:50.298 --> 00:09:53.259
- You know what, yes.

00:09:53.259 --> 00:09:54.635
- Let me check the bottles.

00:09:54.635 --> 00:09:55.511
- Yeah, what do we got?

00:09:55.511 --> 00:10:00.141
- We got a Revana,
which is Napa, and then

00:10:00.141 --> 00:10:02.810
we got Alexana Pinot.

00:10:02.810 --> 00:10:04.020
- I should have known that.

00:10:04.020 --> 00:10:05.354
I appreciate your time.

00:10:05.354 --> 00:10:06.272
This has been great.

00:10:06.272 --> 00:10:07.940
Thank you for being on Full-Bodied.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.609
